      "message": "The specification does not mention waiting for the completed keypress notification on the initiator side; the section 4.2.7.3.2 Authentication stage 1: Passkey Entry Authentication only describes the commitment exchange.\n\nThat will not be an issue as long as the initiator is not the NoInputNoOutput side, all three other cases (Initiator + KeyboardOnly, Responder + KeybordOnly, Responder + NoInputNoOutput) have a clear and linear state machine.\n\nTo resolve the case for the initiator as NoInputNoOutput, the initiator must send LMP_SIMPLE_PAIRING_CONFIRM, then pend for LMP_SIMPLE_PAIRING_CONFIRM response while handling LMP_KEYPRESS_NOTIFICATION in between. No LMP_KEYPRESS_NOTIFICATIONS will be expected after the LMP_SIMPLE_PAIRING_CONFIRM response.",
